00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.540
Leah: Let’s now look at Kanban
starting with its strengths

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.390
Chris: Easy to learn and use -Kanban
is very straightforward with its

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.280
approach and is easy to learn and use.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.519
It can be used in small simple projects
such as for children to help plan

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.150
their homework; to complex business
projects using the Scrum framework.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.500
Leah: Visual-It is a visual system,
and the flow of work is managed

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.370
using a Kanban project board.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.790
In its simplest form there are
three columns which are labelled:

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:34.250
‘To Do’, ‘In Progress’, and ‘Done’.

00:00:35.139 --> 00:00:39.620
Chris: Adaptable and flexible-It
is adaptable and flexible as

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.419
there can be no planned timings
and priorities and workload can

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.240
be changed during the project.

00:00:45.849 --> 00:00:50.280
It is also flexible in that it can be
used with another framework such as Scrum.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:56.070
Leah: Collaborative-As a simple visual
system, it helps the project team to

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.770
collaborate as it simplifies planning,
helps to manage work and inventory, and

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.010
increase productivity and efficiency.

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:07.710
Chris: Low overheads-It has low
overheads as there is no training

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.639
needed and all you need is a Kanban
project board to get started.

00:01:12.699 --> 00:01:15.730
Leah: Reduces costs and waste-As
it can be used with LEAN’s

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:20.780
‘Just In Time’ methodology it
helps to reduce cost and waste.

00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:22.830
Chris: And the Weaknesses

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:28.589
Needs another framework to work-Kanban
would need a framework such as

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:33.280
Scrum or LEAN ‘Just in Time’ to
work as it needs the supporting

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.690
elements that they would give.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.540
Leah: Not suitable on plans that are
not stable-Kanban would need plans

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.740
that are stable and consistent to
work effectively, so this may be an

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.220
issue if the plans need to be dynamic.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:53.340
Chris: Is not Iterative-Another framework
would be needed for iterations to be

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.200
used which would normally end up being
a separate project, as iteration is not

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.510
essential to Kanban at a ticket level.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:05.469
Leah: Lack of timing-Because
Kanban is adaptable and flexible,

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.089
there are often no planned timings
for each stage of the project.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.910
This also means that items can
be changed during the project,

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.860
and this could cause issues.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.519
Chris: A Kanban project could be as
simple as cleaning your house or planning

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.600
school homework or college exams.

00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:26.250
In the workplace examples could include
giving a project manager visibility

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:31.250
to a project status; using a Kanban
board to delegate work across a team;

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.370
or connecting related work items across
different projects or project boards.

